wf-harpoon-turret-unpowered = The turret is dead. No power.
wf-harpoon-turret-cable-attached = The cable is still tied off. Release it first.
wf-harpoon-turret-out-of-arc = The mount will not swing that far.
wf-harpoon-turret-no-cable = No cable is out. Fire a harpoon first.
wf-harpoon-examine-embedded = It is buried in the hull. A crowbar will lever it out.
wf-harpoon-verb-pry = Pry out
wf-harpoon-turret-manned = You take the harpoon turret. Switch to combat mode and click to fire.
wf-harpoon-turret-coil-refused = The tow cable is built into the drum. It takes no coil.
wf-harpoon-turret-examine-powered = It is [color=green]powered[/color].
wf-harpoon-turret-examine-unpowered = It is [color=red]unpowered[/color]. It needs a powered APC nearby before anyone can man it.
wf-harpoon-turret-examine-cable = Its tow cable is built into the drum and ties onto the harpoon when it bites. It takes no coil.
wf-harpoon-turret-examine-fire = Load harpoons by hand, strap in, then switch to combat mode and click to fire. Shots must hit square on to bite.
wf-harpoon-examine-load = Load it into a harpoon turret. The turret's own cable ties onto it when it bites.
wf-harpoon-examine-shields = Harpoons pass straight through ship shields.
